      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "MISS INFORMED (8) made an encouraging return when finishing midfield at Beaudesert and looks set to improve sharply stepping up in distance, and with the blinkers on for the first time. With that first-up run under her belt, she shapes as the one to beat. PIROUETTE GIRL (9) was far from disgraced when finishing fifth at Eagle Farm against stronger opposition a week ago, and if this race has not come too soon for her, she will be hard to hold out. NOZOMU (2) continues to race consistently and was rewarded with another runner-up finish at Ipswich after racing prominently throughout. Expect her to settle on the speed again and she can go one better in this. WELL GROUNDED (6) caught the eye on debut with a strong finish into fifth at the Sunshine Coast, and she is open to plenty of improvement at just her second start. Stick with her. DIAMOND OCEAN (5) has shown enough ability to warrant respect, and he should not be overlooked in an even contest.",
